        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Pain Starvation"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "A specter that goes for more than a month without dealing negative damage to a living humanoid becomes desperate and almost feral. It changes alignment from lawful evil to chaotic evil, loses control of any corrupted thralls it might have, and becomes quickened. It can use its additional action only to make vile touch Strikes against humanoid targets.\n\nAt the end of any turn in which it deals any amount of negative damage to a living humanoid, it reverts to lawful evil and is no longer quickened, but any thralls it lost control of remain free."
            },
            "id": "a41b3ba6-d146-4f0f-b857-a42e7541dda0",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-04-15T14:13:01.456335"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Sunlight Powerlessness"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "A specter caught in sunlight is clumsy 2 and slowed 2 for as long as it remains in the sunlight."
            },
            "id": "6fae4186-3334-415e-bf8d-daabb5de7d4b",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-04-15T14:13:01.456335"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Spectral Corruption"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(curse, divine, enchantment, incapacitation, mental)\n\nWhen the specter damages a living creature with its vile touch Strike, the specter gains 5 temporary Hit Points and the target creature must attempt a 25 Will save to avoid becoming corrupted.\n\n- **Critical Success:** The creature is unaffected and is temporarily immune to spectral corruption for 1 minute.\n- **Success:** The creature is stupefied 2 for 1 hour.\n- **Failure:** The creature succumbs to the corruption and becomes a spectral thrall. The creature is controlled by the specter, obeying the specter's telepathic or spoken orders, though a spectral thrall does not obey obviously self-destructive orders. It can attempt a new Will save at the end of each of its turns; on a success, it is no longer controlled by the specter but becomes stupefied 2 for 1 hour.\n- **Critical Failure:** As failure, but the creature remains a thrall to the specter until the curse is removed or until the specter succumbs to pain starvation; it can't attempt new Will saves to recover on its own. called shiver (Gamemastery Guide"
            },
            "id": "11d7797c-e078-49d1-9ed5-50f10bff861e",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-04-15T14:13:01.456335"
            }
